WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Language models predict plausible text; they do not automatically check the truth. They can quote a repealed rule, mix up procedures from Spain with those in the UK, or treat certain accents and names worse if their data was unbalanced.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:29.300
Responsible use means checking on the official website and saying honestly when a piece of work requires you to declare AI use. Goal: spot jurisdiction hallucinations, bias and transparency duties.

3
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:45.300
An assistant states with great confidence that to work in Manchester you need to «register on the municipal padrón and book an appointment with the EPS». Your task: identify what kind of error happened and where to check the real procedure.

4
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:52.100
Hint: it has mixed institutions from three different countries into one flawless-sounding sentence.

5
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:59.300
Now do the lesson exercises. If you are unsure, watch this video again.
